---
description: Resolve the requested installed unit design and identity work from current native evidence.
args:
  goal: string
returns: UnitHandoffFindings
---
Own the user's unit question and any requested working-only identity draft. Investigate the actual installed inventory and current scoped evidence with investigateUnitHandoff. Let the goal and returned evidence determine which manifest, runtime, artwork or catalog questions need further inspection. An ambiguous name is a reason to explain the ambiguity, not to repurpose another component. Independent read-only inquiries can be composed concurrently; dependent findings and edits must consume their actual basis.

Use reviewIdentity when the requested artwork question or draft needs the installed icon skill. Preserve the original goal, exact requested family and term, current observation and actual native feedback. A catalog alternative is not the same symbol; an unavailable exact request must not be silently replaced. Stage only a user-requested draft whose conditions and current native grant both hold. Permission alone never requests a change. A correct existing icon needs no duplicate edit. A fresh readback does not renew an earlier working-head authorization.

Use completeHandoff to answer the actual question from the acquired observation, design and identity evidence, or compose the equivalent typed findings directly. Return only a real installed unit and an actual verified draft when available. Explain missing evidence and refused or stale edits without claiming that a valid manifest proves a deployed runtime. Protect main, neighboring units and all metadata outside the requested artwork.
